James <james.kanze@gmail.com> wrote:
>IMHO, a Valk can only really be a spellcaster (and not a really
>good one at that) with a robe.

And by the time you set all that up and get your stats raised to the
point where it can be all that useful, you're in the middle to late game
and you ought to have half-a-dozen other ways available to deal with
anything you might deal with using spellcasting. Holy water or various
healing potions are perfectly good emergency alternatives to cure
sickness; you can throw daggers or zap wands instead of using attack
spells; you probably have scrolls or wands of teleportation or even the
Orb of Fate for emergency teleporting; and while +identify is clearly
better than ?identify, you can get by with the latter. It's not like
you're realistically going to be able to cast finger of death anyway.

If you want to be a wizard, play a wizard. :-)

(On cure sickness, admittedly in three valkyrie ascensions I've never
run into Demogorgon, so ...)

